     \[
     R_S(t) = R_1(t) \cdot R_2(t) \cdot R_3(t) \cdot \cdots \cdot R_n(t)
     \]  
   - This is because the sum of the individual relibilities is 1, and the product of the relibilities is 1 when all components are in-use.

b) **Parallel Structure**:  
   - The system fails only if all components fail.  
   - The reliability \( R_S(t) \) is the complement of the probability that all components fail.  
   - If \( R_i(t) \) is the reliability of component \( i \), then:  
     \[
     R_S(t) = 1 - (1 - R_1(t)) \cdot (1 - R_2(t)) \cdot (1 - R_3(t)) \cdot \cdots \cdot (1 - R_n(t))
     \]  
