","The key difference between σ (sigma) and π (pi) molecular orbitals lies in the electron density distribution:  
- **σ molecular orbitals** have electron density concentrated along the axis between the nuclei of the bonded atoms. The σ orbital is formed by head-on overlap of atomic orbitals, resulting in a symmetrical electron density distribution.  
- **π molecular orbitals** have electron density concentrated above and below the axis between the nuclei of the bonded atoms. The π orbital is formed by side-by-side overlap of atomic orbitals, resulting in a nodal plane (zero electron density) along the axis between the nuclei.  

