Dave walks to his friend's house with an average of 80 steps per minute, and each step measures 65 cm. It takes him 20 minutes to get there. Meanwhile, his sister, Lucy, uses the same path to reach the same destination. Lucy averages 90 steps per minute, with each step measuring 55 cm long. How long does it take Lucy to get to the friend's house?
$\mathrm{(A) \ } 18 \text{minutes} \qquad \mathrm{(B) \ } 19.5 \text{minutes}\qquad \mathrm{(C) \ } 21 \text{minutes} \qquad \mathrm{(D) \ } 22.5 \text{minutes} \qquad \mathrm{(E) \ } 24 \text{minutes}$
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
1. **Calculate the total steps for Dave:**  
   \(80 \text{ steps/min} \times 20 \text{ min} = 1600 \text{ steps}\)

2. **Calculate the total distance for Dave:**  
   \(1600 \text{ steps} \times 65 \text{ cm/step} = 102,400 \text{ cm}\)  
   Convert to meters: \(102,400 \text{ cm} = 1024 \text{ m}\)

3. **Calculate the speed for Lucy (speed = distance / time):**  
   \(1024 \text{ m} = 1024 \text{ m} \times \frac{1 \text{ day}}{24 \text{ hr}} \times \frac{1 \text{ hr}}{3600 \text{ s}} = 1.1 \text{ s}\)  
   \(1.1 \text{ s} \times 90 \text{ steps/min} = 109 \text{ steps/min}\)

4. **Calculate the time for Lucy:**  
   \(1600 \text{ steps} \div 90 \text{ steps/min} = 17.78 \text{ min}\)  
   Round to the nearest minute: \(\boxed{18 \text{ minutes}}\)

</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

