   \[
   \int_{-1}^{2} (x^2 + 2) \, dx = \left. \left[ \frac{x^3}{3} + 2x \right] \right\limits_{-1}^{2}
   \]

3. **Evaluate the definite integral:**
   \[
   \left. \left[ \frac{x^3}{3} + 2x \right] \right\limits_{-1}^{2} = \left( \frac{2^3}{3} + 2 \cdot 2 \right) - \left( \frac{-1^3}{3} + 2 \cdot (-1) \right)
