c) A new study is underway to track the eating and exercise patterns of people at different time-periods in the future, and see who is afflicted with cancer later in life.  
d) The prices of generic items are compared to the prices of the equivalent named brand items.
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
a) **Retrospective**  
   - The study examines current or previous smoking habits of people who already have a characteristic (bladder cancer).  

b) **Cross-sectional**  
   - The study gathers information about eating habits and general health at a single point in time.  

c) **Prospective**  
   - The study observes the eating and exercise patterns of the population over time to predict future cancer development.  

d) **Comparative/Not Temporal**  
   - The study does not involve time progression. It directly compares two data points (prices of generic vs. non-general goods) at a single point of time.  

Thus, d is not classified as cross-sectional, retrospective, or prospective.  

\boxed{a} \text{ Retrospective} & \boxed{b} \text{ Cross-sectional} & \boxed{c} \text{ Prospective} & \boxed{d} \text{ Comparative}

