<start_of_turn>model
","1. **Calculate the mass of the satellite**:  
   The gravitational force \( F = mg \), so:  
   \[
   m = \frac{F}{g} = \frac{3600 \text{ N}}{9 \text{ m/s}^2} = 400 \text{ kg}
   \]

2. **Calculate the kinetic energy**:  
   The kinetic energy \( KE = \frac{1}{2} mv^2 \), so:  
   \[
   KE = \frac{1}{2} \times 400 \text{ kg} \times (800 \text{ m/s})^2 = 1260000 \text{ J} = 1.26 \times 10^6 \text{ J}
   \]

   The kinetic energy of the satellite is \(\boxed{1.26 \times 10^6 \text{ J}}\).
