\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \frac{\partial \phi}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial \psi}{\partial x} \mathbf{k}
\]
Thus, the curl of \(\mathbf{V}(x, y)\) is:
\[
\boxed{\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \frac{\partial \phi}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial \psi}{\partial x} \mathbf{k}}
