\]

The absolute value of the work is \( 1.75 \times 10^3 \) bar·L. Converting to joules (1 bar·L = 100 J):

\[
1.75 \times 10^3 \text{ bar} \cdot \text{L} \times 100 \text{ J/(bar} \cdot \text{L)} = 1.75 \times 10^5 \text{ J}.
\]

Now, calculate the mass of TNT required to release the same energy (4680 J/g TNT):

\[
