","The entropy production rate \( \Pi_S \) is given by:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{d \Delta S}{dt} = \frac{Q}{T}
\]
where \( Q \) is the rate of heat transfer and \( T \) is the temperature. The heat transfer \( Q \) is due to the work done by the friction force \( F_{\text{fr}} \) over the relative velocity \( v \):
\[
Q = F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v
\]
Thus, the entropy production rate is:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v}{T}
\]
The final answer is:
\[
\boxed{\Pi_S = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v}{T}}
\]
